values ('a5b6c7d8-9e0f-4a47-8b77-7c8d9e0f1a97', 'microeconomics-macroeconomics', 'Microeconomics / Macroeconomics', 'This course integrates microeconomic and macroeconomic reasoning for business, supply-chain, and policy decision-making. Students learn how markets coordinate choices, how firms set prices and compete, when markets fail, how the national and global economy is measured, how policy affects inflation, employment, growth, exchange rates, and financial conditions, and how economic data can support managerial decisions. The course emphasizes rigorous models, data interpretation, strategic application, and clear communication.');

