  'Microeconomics / Macroeconomics',
  'This course integrates microeconomic and macroeconomic reasoning for business, supply-chain, and policy decision-making. Students learn how markets coordinate choices, how firms set prices and compete, when markets fail, how the national and global economy is measured, how policy affects inflation, employment, growth, exchange rates, and financial conditions, and how economic data can support managerial decisions. The course emphasizes rigorous models, data interpretation, strategic application, and clear communication.',
  $mmecjson${"slug": "microeconomics-macroeconomics", "title": "Microeconomics / Macroeconomics", "description": "This course integrates microeconomic and macroeconomic reasoning for business, supply-chain, and policy decision-making. Students learn how markets coordinate choices, how firms set prices and compete, when markets fail, how the national and global economy is measured, how policy affects inflation, employment, growth, exchange rates, and financial conditions, and how economic data can support managerial decisions. The course emphasizes rigorous models, data interpretation, strategic application, and clear communication.", "topics": [{"id": "7f3a1b29-c1f6-452e-a053-cd7194b6505f", "type": "topic", "title": "Economic Thinking: Scarcity, Incentives, and Models", "description": "This opening topic teaches students how economists simplify complex decisions into models while staying alert to assumptions and limits.", "children": [{"id": "b4569cc9-71b1-4f26-a944-c92a07f642bb", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Scarcity and opportunity cost", "children": [{"id": "d594dac3-3e9d-4f6d-b4a8-1277af15887f", "type": "concept", "title": "Production possibilities"}, {"id": "56bea888-cca8-4dce-9cb8-718eb14e7679", "type": "concept", "title": "Marginal thinking"}, {"id": "18e3e512-f96f-496f-8421-220da594cecd", "type": "concept", "title": "Sunk costs versus opportunity costs"}], "description": "Students learn why every business, policy, and household choice has a tradeoff."}, {"id": "02d2ea5d-47a2-4210-bd2e-5a2b5f7f9aac", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Incentives and behavior", "children": [{"id": "189bd10d-1323-427f-ac63-caa4e9922fac", "type": "concept", "title": "Positive and negative incentives"}, {"id": "88cc865d-b72f-4bea-90f6-5eb2235fd639", "type": "concept", "title": "Unintended consequences"}, {"id": "4da84d05-2e26-4853-b016-577f3f797311", "type": "concept", "title": "Institutional constraints"}], "description": "The point is to see prices, rules, contracts, and norms as signals that shape choices."}, {"id": "7c15cd90-18b2-44d8-88b9-38b102ce4480", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Economic models and evidence", "children": [{"id": "31b61054-e095-4763-a63e-f3c2f4421e25", "type": "concept", "title": "Ceteris paribus reasoning"}, {"id": "54b8ebe3-56ed-455c-a086-ad07ed7ed1be", "type": "concept", "title": "Graphs and equations"}, {"id": "1a5afd12-0b6c-4866-bacb-7b7759a9ed2c", "type": "concept", "title": "Model assumptions and empirical checks"}], "description": "Students learn to use models as disciplined thinking tools, not as mechanical answers."}]}, {"id": "62a43a66-e906-48c9-b491-2fe3b14eda25", "type": "topic", "title": "Supply, Demand, and Market Equilibrium", "description": "Supply and demand are the foundation for understanding prices, shortages, surpluses, and adjustment in product, labor, and input markets.", "children": [{"id": "0f3c2f4d-4e71-47ca-9435-162f60912458", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Demand and willingness to pay", "children": [{"id": "432732f9-862f-42fb-bbdc-f847c8423ffc", "type": "concept", "title": "Movement along demand versus shifts"}, {"id": "5185265d-c660-4109-abaf-72d142ffa5c8", "type": "concept", "title": "Consumer surplus"}, {"id": "ccdba3b7-5e7b-4177-a2ef-8ac8e46956f1", "type": "concept", "title": "Demand shocks"}], "description": "Students connect demand curves to consumer value, substitutes, complements, income, and expectations."}, {"id": "b04602cc-cd82-4dc5-add2-31aa19fd540d", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Supply and willingness to sell", "children": [{"id": "fb939e0b-29c0-48b7-ab50-99bab52409aa", "type": "concept", "title": "Movement along supply versus shifts"}, {"id": "ca03523f-632a-4955-8c4f-20dbc5c186fe", "type": "concept", "title": "Producer surplus"}, {"id": "6d038dc7-53a9-4e92-bc12-97b1ecd063ba", "type": "concept", "title": "Supply shocks"}], "description": "Students learn how costs, technology, capacity, and input prices shape supply."}, {"id": "1dfd2978-f445-497f-b3a9-b57f776f043b", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Equilibrium and market adjustment", "children": [{"id": "2b780023-2ff5-4104-964d-6dabdedcf6e1", "type": "concept", "title": "Shortage and surplus"}, {"id": "140bb2b7-cf68-4f04-9b92-e18423fc6212", "type": "concept", "title": "Comparative statics"}, {"id": "a240011d-f0c3-4817-8a6a-e1fd8cfc198e", "type": "concept", "title": "Price controls and rationing"}], "description": "The gist is to understand how decentralized decisions coordinate through prices."}]}, {"id": "bfd93e2d-9401-4767-971b-6c97d3cd4bbf", "type": "topic", "title": "Elasticity, Revenue, and Business Decision-Making", "description": "Elasticity turns market intuition into practical pricing, forecasting, and policy analysis.", "children": [{"id": "513e72e2-f5f6-42f2-b9a4-97cb8c911138", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Price elasticity of demand", "children": [{"id": "3128e631-9059-42d4-a7b0-d62544bee503", "type": "concept", "title": "Elastic, inelastic, and unit elastic demand"}, {"id": "49b3cee9-213f-4da2-a0a6-23d45dbb89ae", "type": "concept", "title": "Total revenue test"}, {"id": "a3fe4e78-4e74-4151-a3c2-5b7b33a6017d", "type": "concept", "title": "Determinants of elasticity"}], "description": "Students learn how quantity responds to price changes and why revenue may rise or fall."}, {"id": "5a08d7e0-a98a-4f94-b8c4-1c4b16b4ef1f", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Other elasticities", "children": [{"id": "c63c3a0d-30b0-4308-a66f-51e31f98e720", "type": "concept", "title": "Income elasticity"}, {"id": "9bc75dcb-fe50-4a52-b03e-63e0964a14a8", "type": "concept", "title": "Cross-price elasticity"}, {"id": "c2089c0e-43ce-4423-88c9-4e725c028227", "type": "concept", "title": "Price elasticity of supply"}], "description": "The point is to connect markets across products, income groups, and supply conditions."}, {"id": "7996217e-65a4-4c81-aa7b-8acac8a54d32", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Business and supply-chain uses", "children": [{"id": "69874de8-2c81-4e11-a935-0bca4967a143", "type": "concept", "title": "Demand forecasting"}, {"id": "75237524-7dae-4c0a-afaf-50d897e231e0", "type": "concept", "title": "Pass-through of cost shocks"}, {"id": "10ae62af-a2fe-4b78-9fa7-83a0eb19fe90", "type": "concept", "title": "Pricing experiments"}], "description": "Students apply elasticity to pricing, procurement, inventory, capacity, and promotion decisions."}]}, {"id": "3ed820a9-ec79-4568-9f50-c3c4dccbd604", "type": "topic", "title": "Consumer Choice, Utility, and Behavioral Economics", "description": "This topic explains demand from the inside: preferences, constraints, judgment, bias, and actual human behavior.", "children": [{"id": "a3e9f924-a989-4a3f-8d7d-0504b5bce014", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Utility and constraints", "children": [{"id": "92628485-5a38-41b5-8993-b08b00ec4149", "type": "concept", "title": "Budget constraints"}, {"id": "b4af4214-14a0-4704-9d61-25133f64faee", "type": "concept", "title": "Marginal utility"}, {"id": "fc6db72b-8e0d-432e-a388-f73c0bdad209", "type": "concept", "title": "Substitution and income effects"}], "description": "Students learn how consumers allocate scarce income across competing wants."}, {"id": "b0612b8b-6ea0-4874-89e5-a396e58b6b83", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Demand estimation and segmentation", "children": [{"id": "c66d7ff3-dd92-4db2-bdfa-8e5904ffbc66", "type": "concept", "title": "Revealed preference"}, {"id": "5598fd94-dc5e-43db-b879-08bf4e862362", "type": "concept", "title": "Customer heterogeneity"}, {"id": "6fa38559-c74c-4cc6-8dda-9675add30344", "type": "concept", "title": "Willingness to pay"}], "description": "The gist is to link theory to observed purchasing behavior."}, {"id": "6eabb80a-1bd7-4f14-bcd1-2cef6b4eff87", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Behavioral economics", "children": [{"id": "defd8b87-1a3f-463f-b63e-f4f078f19b24", "type": "concept", "title": "Loss aversion"}, {"id": "68c8ebd5-06a3-4281-9c67-5f0807e7132a", "type": "concept", "title": "Framing and defaults"}, {"id": "d3c822b2-974d-4a61-993e-7919e35bbf10", "type": "concept", "title": "Present bias and heuristics"}], "description": "Students learn where real decision-making departs from simple rational-agent assumptions."}]}, {"id": "cbcc05e2-d3c4-4fe0-9bdc-c7cdf88eab0b", "type": "topic", "title": "Firms, Production, Costs, and Supply Chains", "description": "Students learn how firms transform inputs into outputs and how cost structure shapes pricing, sourcing, and scale decisions.", "children": [{"id": "1602644b-4dc4-429c-877c-968a53143aff", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Production and productivity", "children": [{"id": "9c0feb98-a794-4fa1-a9a0-b2db8931e635", "type": "concept", "title": "Production functions"}, {"id": "21565deb-25ef-4349-9604-603f96cd3c8f", "type": "concept", "title": "Marginal product"}, {"id": "e86a6a3d-c9d0-45c9-954d-5a06f54d6f5c", "type": "concept", "title": "Returns to scale"}], "description": "The point is to connect inputs, technology, labor, and capital to output."}, {"id": "c1acce31-c4b6-4abb-9fe4-3c52507ac254", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Cost theory", "children": [{"id": "85bfb991-4ccf-4207-9974-62834954d605", "type": "concept", "title": "Economies and diseconomies of scale"}, {"id": "cebdab74-4d58-4662-8b9f-92014b4c0d6b", "type": "concept", "title": "Learning curves"}, {"id": "ad026317-5592-4f58-a3e2-cc5639e33ec0", "type": "concept", "title": "Shutdown and exit conditions"}], "description": "Students distinguish fixed, variable, marginal, average, short-run, and long-run costs."}, {"id": "90b2fe69-63b0-4a0f-a5ca-83a8f9f34ebe", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Supply-chain cost decisions", "children": [{"id": "06fdf82b-9575-4478-a5b2-33ebab2f9100", "type": "concept", "title": "Inventory and carrying cost"}, {"id": "9d8a79f8-d080-42e1-b9c9-b7722f853a49", "type": "concept", "title": "Supplier market power"}, {"id": "fdc81fd8-12c0-4529-9ce5-ba87b61cb751", "type": "concept", "title": "Transportation and location tradeoffs"}], "description": "Students apply cost thinking to make-versus-buy, capacity, logistics, and sourcing."}]}, {"id": "e1a23d03-c2d6-475a-96e9-d999ead58110", "type": "topic", "title": "Market Structures and Competitive Strategy", "description": "Market structure shapes pricing power, strategic behavior, innovation, and welfare.", "children": [{"id": "81e95195-b349-4678-9843-1201f70ed57c", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Perfect competition and monopoly", "children": [{"id": "3666f70a-a0b9-482e-b1e4-a5056869bd14", "type": "concept", "title": "Profit maximization"}, {"id": "74e3b67a-bc39-47f4-bf19-183e872ffca4", "type": "concept", "title": "Deadweight loss"}, {"id": "885d9a01-0efa-420f-8714-b4a5ae5c7dd5", "type": "concept", "title": "Natural monopoly"}], "description": "Students contrast price-taking markets with single-seller market power."}, {"id": "b10bad46-5404-4aee-9f80-449c06cc0a33", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Monopolistic competition and oligopoly", "children": [{"id": "d3281901-199e-4562-98dc-c9aecd27b7fc", "type": "concept", "title": "Product differentiation"}, {"id": "31c36108-a2e3-4a29-ae8a-bbc9026f13f1", "type": "concept", "title": "Entry and exit"}, {"id": "ab6dca52-1c2c-48be-a359-dba8dc2620de", "type": "concept", "title": "Strategic complements and substitutes"}], "description": "The gist is to analyze differentiation, rivalry, and interdependence."}, {"id": "2a6a449e-7cea-49a1-9a70-8eca99476d05", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Pricing and revenue strategy", "children": [{"id": "83a13176-45f2-4d90-9de1-2ff35191a33d", "type": "concept", "title": "Price discrimination"}, {"id": "26c83ec3-c49f-419c-97dd-26b0bc013148", "type": "concept", "title": "Bundling and versioning"}, {"id": "7daab87e-e894-401e-9312-d10417bf6d7a", "type": "concept", "title": "Revenue optimization"}], "description": "Students apply microeconomic logic to business pricing."}]}, {"id": "032ba155-86d0-464e-baeb-5430d376ea5d", "type": "topic", "title": "Game Theory, Platforms, and Strategic Interaction", "description": "This unit adds strategic reasoning for markets where outcomes depend on rivals, partners, customers, and network effects.", "children": [{"id": "543e93e0-bec7-453c-8f62-555bc3466e69", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Game theory basics", "children": [{"id": "36b164dc-ba55-40ae-aafd-f170b4f56fa5", "type": "concept", "title": "Dominant strategies"}, {"id": "7006d692-acf1-45ed-a723-e274e37e0685", "type": "concept", "title": "Nash equilibrium"}, {"id": "4176f390-0fb0-465d-852e-d3d31a212aba", "type": "concept", "title": "Sequential games"}], "description": "Students learn to model interdependent decisions."}, {"id": "cbeff9cf-3bfe-4b37-b265-c043bd6b45e2", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Strategic competition", "children": [{"id": "c32614e3-281d-4951-a91e-c99006c342e3", "type": "concept", "title": "Prisoner's dilemma"}, {"id": "75c9f0e1-efc9-4d97-8588-e7235e95c56a", "type": "concept", "title": "Repeated games"}, {"id": "27c18e47-6b9b-40b8-a20c-7bd9f0db9149", "type": "concept", "title": "Commitment and signaling"}], "description": "The point is to understand price wars, entry deterrence, cooperation, and credible commitment."}, {"id": "ebe1e47b-b150-4731-a9f4-5a6711f7a040", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Platforms and network effects", "children": [{"id": "ebb66b0b-d992-47b5-bade-9efaaf0a7094", "type": "concept", "title": "Direct and indirect network effects"}, {"id": "5174f9ef-8f57-4400-aa67-355caf5d9aa5", "type": "concept", "title": "Subsidizing one side of the market"}, {"id": "62251d3b-9d7a-445b-907d-ec7955d13dd8", "type": "concept", "title": "Winner-take-most dynamics"}], "description": "Students examine two-sided markets and digital business models."}]}, {"id": "b1e9c6fd-12b7-4ecd-9619-35c44f769e04", "type": "topic", "title": "Market Failures, Externalities, Public Goods, and Policy", "description": "Students learn when markets fail to allocate resources efficiently and what policy tools can improve or worsen outcomes.", "children": [{"id": "fb33bf28-dbb2-43ec-82f8-037c5cbb74f2", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Externalities", "children": [{"id": "3a0447b3-9108-4111-84c4-db694addfb2a", "type": "concept", "title": "Pollution and congestion"}, {"id": "ea73c624-147d-4caa-b4a1-6d81ab298077", "type": "concept", "title": "Pigouvian taxes and subsidies"}, {"id": "b90eed06-5625-4acd-9214-80e88ca6b10e", "type": "concept", "title": "Cap-and-trade"}], "description": "Students identify costs or benefits not reflected in market prices."}, {"id": "6e6175d0-5d1e-4b55-be11-de2e963ef141", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Public goods and common resources", "children": [{"id": "99fc426f-fa23-4f44-85b3-daeeb951b52a", "type": "concept", "title": "Nonrivalry and nonexcludability"}, {"id": "8762e269-3f06-4c85-a6db-4f72a26b72ac", "type": "concept", "title": "Tragedy of the commons"}, {"id": "83197305-fbd4-4be5-8e4e-262720d8af5a", "type": "concept", "title": "Collective action"}], "description": "The point is to understand free riding, nonexcludability, and overuse."}, {"id": "c4c612b8-d38e-4dbc-977f-dec016420075", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Regulation and antitrust", "children": [{"id": "ee6ba850-b565-4094-98ec-305506fd5bf6", "type": "concept", "title": "Information disclosure"}, {"id": "638702b9-81d2-4b33-9a32-0c8f2d156c12", "type": "concept", "title": "Competition policy"}, {"id": "705d767f-149d-48d1-adef-df32a55de8d5", "type": "concept", "title": "Regulatory tradeoffs"}], "description": "Students examine policy responses to monopoly power, asymmetric information, and market design problems."}]}, {"id": "e5b53fe9-5a35-4cc0-8e46-0ab99d1b07bf", "type": "topic", "title": "Measuring the Macroeconomy: GDP, Prices, Labor, and Data", "description": "Macroeconomics begins with measurement: students learn what the headline indicators mean and what they miss.", "children": [{"id": "f1139eca-0b7e-44a3-8b79-b1bef8980979", "type": "subtopic", "title": "National income accounting", "children": [{"id": "e18b67af-9dcc-4abc-ad48-6e63cb3477df", "type": "concept", "title": "GDP, GNP, GNI, and value added"}, {"id": "65240fec-f7a4-4512-b3cb-e3d579a59bbc", "type": "concept", "title": "Nominal versus real GDP"}, {"id": "3dea5275-5079-490c-b321-ca26c951e3f5", "type": "concept", "title": "Limits of GDP"}], "description": "Students learn how GDP and related measures track production and income."}, {"id": "ebafdcd2-5301-4d48-95ce-12cf8608e24c", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Inflation and price indexes", "children": [{"id": "05dd7cd3-0604-4bd7-bfef-7794074d522e", "type": "concept", "title": "CPI and PCE"}, {"id": "74540d66-e502-4d09-8e13-ab77c6588e85", "type": "concept", "title": "Real versus nominal values"}, {"id": "797a07d1-5122-440b-b797-5ac52f466b2c", "type": "concept", "title": "Cost-of-living measurement issues"}], "description": "The gist is to measure changes in the purchasing power of money."}, {"id": "cd67a8de-0748-4dce-b911-9fdbcc729c64", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Labor market indicators", "children": [{"id": "23c75d60-e28b-41d8-959c-078719609f26", "type": "concept", "title": "Unemployment types"}, {"id": "493b55a6-288c-43c7-8d94-ed94b2872887", "type": "concept", "title": "Participation and discouraged workers"}, {"id": "debf42a1-5924-4f84-a8db-88afb395fda9", "type": "concept", "title": "Wage growth and productivity"}], "description": "Students learn to interpret unemployment, labor force participation, wages, and productivity."}]}, {"id": "ff321978-654a-4c15-b03a-353cdcbb73db", "type": "topic", "title": "Long-Run Growth, Productivity, and Living Standards", "description": "This topic explains why some economies become richer over time and why growth matters for firms, workers, and governments.", "children": [{"id": "9936af25-7e01-45f3-a551-79e8e756e6c1", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Sources of growth", "children": [{"id": "d768f88a-2407-4a6b-8768-287b6d3fcc13", "type": "concept", "title": "Capital deepening"}, {"id": "1c823e57-3a21-4cd5-bead-a374888a0e6a", "type": "concept", "title": "Human capital"}, {"id": "b4dcb4fa-1e7c-40e8-9563-21008f5f8956", "type": "concept", "title": "Total factor productivity"}], "description": "Students connect output per person to labor, capital, technology, and institutions."}, {"id": "f46d6d6d-1cf5-4b22-b074-337eaa7f9cbe", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Institutions and innovation", "children": [{"id": "9a174221-9dae-4a0b-8b79-3add1993279b", "type": "concept", "title": "Property rights"}, {"id": "19d26506-1ec3-4993-bbe4-8ad15e1366b6", "type": "concept", "title": "Markets and competition"}, {"id": "b7d578ab-f48e-45fa-82aa-4c1801f154a8", "type": "concept", "title": "Research, entrepreneurship, and diffusion"}], "description": "The point is to see growth as more than accumulation."}, {"id": "0ee08631-6a8b-40b2-b3c4-49b0b3cd1603", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Inequality and inclusive growth", "children": [{"id": "ea790821-6662-497c-ae4e-58f976579c7c", "type": "concept", "title": "Income and wealth inequality"}, {"id": "52f2548a-698e-450b-bbca-428e49f2c2a2", "type": "concept", "title": "Mobility"}, {"id": "b0dd77c4-3e6a-409c-ab90-914082909a3e", "type": "concept", "title": "Policy and human development"}], "description": "Students analyze who benefits from growth and why distribution matters."}]}, {"id": "4a4c4d4c-e58e-4014-bdc6-9b9ea714692a", "type": "topic", "title": "Business Cycles, Aggregate Demand, and Aggregate Supply", "description": "Students learn why economies expand and contract and how shocks move through output, employment, prices, and expectations.", "children": [{"id": "b835d565-0e2b-41f2-b58e-c68dcc122c5e", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Business cycle indicators", "children": [{"id": "2441765b-f15c-49c6-b0d5-12be19b40203", "type": "concept", "title": "Output gap"}, {"id": "87443e9c-d92e-4993-8c18-1470523d2b18", "type": "concept", "title": "Labor market slack"}, {"id": "219f4539-1c22-431c-852b-ac386db0bda9", "type": "concept", "title": "Confidence and financial conditions"}], "description": "Students identify expansions, recessions, peaks, troughs, and leading indicators."}, {"id": "3c96cad4-a7c9-4067-b4cd-b973b7e5570d", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Aggregate demand", "children": [{"id": "b0207909-2892-4bad-a223-3a69a4f4883b", "type": "concept", "title": "Consumption"}, {"id": "e772ddad-bf7d-434e-8303-2d3f74228642", "type": "concept", "title": "Investment"}, {"id": "748db734-1f3c-4978-a222-ef2f1998d576", "type": "concept", "title": "Government spending and net exports"}], "description": "The gist is to understand spending by households, firms, government, and foreign buyers."}, {"id": "8eea1c4c-328c-45a0-804f-d3f4238fd457", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Aggregate supply", "children": [{"id": "1ad0a6cc-e29f-46de-8f36-a38cc8eb3932", "type": "concept", "title": "Short-run versus long-run aggregate supply"}, {"id": "5b2a0618-de35-4256-80b5-f7e26ec60d61", "type": "concept", "title": "Supply shocks"}, {"id": "5aca7b58-a7d3-433f-a557-8b1e847ffebe", "type": "concept", "title": "Stagflation"}], "description": "Students connect production capacity, input costs, productivity, and price adjustment."}]}, {"id": "425f6293-6fbf-47f4-b024-358cc13457d1", "type": "topic", "title": "Fiscal Policy, Public Debt, and Stabilization", "description": "Fiscal policy uses taxes, transfers, and spending to influence demand, distribution, public goods, and long-run capacity.", "children": [{"id": "bc29beb2-d9df-431d-9344-650f333bbeaf", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Government budgets", "children": [{"id": "77f08e60-a6a4-4a08-a304-3d65f0f1d6bd", "type": "concept", "title": "Budget balance"}, {"id": "3c851aa0-33da-44de-a313-4000ed03ce01", "type": "concept", "title": "Debt-to-GDP"}, {"id": "bf61c110-304d-4b8e-aecd-caa013f3c415", "type": "concept", "title": "Automatic versus discretionary policy"}], "description": "Students learn how deficits, debt, and automatic stabilizers work."}, {"id": "27efb8dc-a217-4f6d-a5f4-43f7b10294ea", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Fiscal multipliers", "children": [{"id": "419f6fe8-ab4b-4a33-a1b0-b4dc3bb4167c", "type": "concept", "title": "Marginal propensity to consume"}, {"id": "04f81142-83f2-4801-bd3c-662704c6c8c0", "type": "concept", "title": "Crowding out"}, {"id": "6c137fff-4192-404f-95f0-75f2cd6c83b6", "type": "concept", "title": "State-dependent multipliers"}], "description": "The point is to evaluate when spending or tax changes have large or small effects."}, {"id": "e25ec288-2b3b-4fd5-9cd3-5dbc5e146527", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Policy tradeoffs", "children": [{"id": "83b53fba-185a-4b40-85f0-472add4d5f69", "type": "concept", "title": "Stimulus versus austerity"}, {"id": "0d2e9c68-ba8f-45b7-8f6d-393047febde4", "type": "concept", "title": "Public investment"}, {"id": "bbb1b5cd-72ae-4f25-9f81-e9f738043d81", "type": "concept", "title": "Intergenerational burden"}], "description": "Students examine short-run stabilization alongside long-run sustainability and equity."}]}, {"id": "eabe518c-4357-4047-812b-1861c8f3b46c", "type": "topic", "title": "Money, Banking, Central Banks, and Monetary Policy", "description": "Students learn how money, banks, interest rates, and central banks shape spending, inflation, credit, and financial stability.", "children": [{"id": "2f142782-c51e-4a67-858d-006c6aa140c3", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Money and banking", "children": [{"id": "660a3a20-6e00-4e05-9ad7-2c41275a05db", "type": "concept", "title": "Functions of money"}, {"id": "140c9210-b8e1-41af-a701-06e8c64b59bb", "type": "concept", "title": "Bank balance sheets"}, {"id": "061f0d8c-5386-4c22-8bd1-27961fbcedff", "type": "concept", "title": "Money creation and credit"}], "description": "Students understand the role of money, deposits, lending, and financial intermediation."}, {"id": "feccecf2-283f-40ee-ab80-b437a25208e1", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Central bank tools", "children": [{"id": "3cb4ae24-774a-4b5e-916c-57fdea366f60", "type": "concept", "title": "Policy rates"}, {"id": "532f53d2-f35b-4598-bad1-04bd7f89fa80", "type": "concept", "title": "Open-market operations"}, {"id": "e49228e7-b6fc-4560-b652-ec31949245f3", "type": "concept", "title": "Quantitative easing and balance sheets"}], "description": "The gist is to connect policy instruments to financial conditions."}, {"id": "18101c4c-ed79-4367-bf00-51b8cef9f0bf", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Inflation and monetary transmission", "children": [{"id": "3ecc68ea-0767-446b-addd-12ffada97bd8", "type": "concept", "title": "Taylor rule intuition"}, {"id": "1c4785ca-0e23-41b9-8a49-7485e388f04e", "type": "concept", "title": "Phillips curve"}, {"id": "c5d7e956-c275-4808-9c91-b332e8469833", "type": "concept", "title": "Lags and credibility"}], "description": "Students learn how monetary policy affects demand, expectations, and prices."}]}, {"id": "8e4acbc8-5554-4697-a847-b7756d990bfe", "type": "topic", "title": "International Trade, Exchange Rates, and Global Supply Chains", "description": "This unit links economic foundations to global sourcing, trade policy, exchange rates, and supply-chain risk.", "children": [{"id": "43b0eab8-f485-471c-81c0-76cc495febee", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Comparative advantage and gains from trade", "children": [{"id": "a4749c4c-2820-4385-94c6-1e54d78c3891", "type": "concept", "title": "Opportunity cost"}, {"id": "a1a02830-3683-4042-a329-5d7898b1a654", "type": "concept", "title": "Specialization"}, {"id": "08fbc555-a418-4ead-8bf0-f0da47efad8a", "type": "concept", "title": "Winners and losers"}], "description": "Students learn why trade can raise total welfare while creating distributional conflict."}, {"id": "7f66431c-a57b-4885-9706-65207668a670", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Trade policy and global value chains", "children": [{"id": "d40c91c5-a84f-484f-be7e-ad1d967c21e5", "type": "concept", "title": "Tariffs and deadweight loss"}, {"id": "2aae0ddc-8901-4c2d-8c4b-5216296262bf", "type": "concept", "title": "Rules of origin"}, {"id": "e5f80dd7-9e9f-40cf-b6cc-513fcac358a5", "type": "concept", "title": "Reshoring and friend-shoring"}], "description": "The point is to understand tariffs, quotas, trade agreements, and supply-chain exposure."}, {"id": "2e293ca7-26ab-49a7-bf10-6b506044f02d", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Exchange rates and balance of payments", "children": [{"id": "92ffcf8c-5ad5-4261-994e-1aeab8b9a5d5", "type": "concept", "title": "Nominal and real exchange rates"}, {"id": "41db429a-e23d-4b69-8441-38fec19d0932", "type": "concept", "title": "Appreciation and depreciation"}, {"id": "436e6ae4-7568-49de-9cff-4878ae903274", "type": "concept", "title": "Current and capital accounts"}], "description": "Students learn how currency changes affect import costs, export competitiveness, and financial exposure."}]}, {"id": "88f9ce4a-c815-450c-8d5f-e3780bd9bd01", "type": "topic", "title": "Global Business Environment, Geopolitics, and Scenario Planning", "description": null, "children": [{"id": "781e5b52-f38b-4bb8-8b27-c7967664568a", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Country and sovereign risk", "children": [{"id": "cbedfbc4-3b9f-44bb-a4b8-c6dc174387ae", "type": "concept", "title": "Inflation and debt stress"}, {"id": "f39b5cf3-96e2-4866-ad70-0f33dd3b04ef", "type": "concept", "title": "Political risk"}, {"id": "7b01d3c9-397b-46bd-8785-dfd032bedb80", "type": "concept", "title": "Capital controls and default risk"}], "description": "Students connect macro indicators to business risk."}, {"id": "974d9361-ec0e-4450-94bb-81e97bbbd872", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Global shocks and crises", "children": [{"id": "b3301ef6-4a1e-4994-84bf-abcf7bdf35d7", "type": "concept", "title": "Financial crises"}, {"id": "47755e76-a77d-4fe6-b2de-78e6cb82ae34", "type": "concept", "title": "Pandemics and supply shocks"}, {"id": "0c412483-f3f7-4224-a966-8782632fd958", "type": "concept", "title": "Commodity and energy shocks"}], "description": "The gist is to analyze disruptions to energy, credit, supply chains, trade, and confidence."}, {"id": "42934b07-81ea-4239-a709-d3dc1c972b88", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Scenario planning", "children": [{"id": "34474646-4297-4864-a72a-983ed7a40985", "type": "concept", "title": "Base, upside, and downside cases"}, {"id": "b7a4615d-f6b9-4969-aee0-092e07a51bdd", "type": "concept", "title": "Early warning indicators"}, {"id": "ff55bf9e-ab53-4c73-8d16-e8f62a4033dd", "type": "concept", "title": "Decision triggers"}], "description": "Students translate economic uncertainty into strategic options."}]}, {"id": "f1d8bf6c-496b-475d-b04a-29c7071e1a72", "type": "topic", "title": "Data-Driven Economic Analysis and Policy Evaluation", "description": "Students practice using economic data to test claims, make charts, and support business or policy recommendations.", "children": [{"id": "af8a138e-ea31-41f3-9d33-7d02574f1114", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Working with economic data", "children": [{"id": "900f9a18-9978-481f-ab54-2dd4e348b72c", "type": "concept", "title": "Time series"}, {"id": "caa37b12-f8d1-4a6b-8ae6-33764e7a1781", "type": "concept", "title": "Indexing and transformations"}, {"id": "dd035cee-7e5f-4759-bb7a-c84daaa0e31b", "type": "concept", "title": "Real, nominal, and per-capita adjustments"}], "description": "Students learn to retrieve and interpret data from sources such as FRED, BEA, IMF, and World Bank."}, {"id": "8883227b-f15c-4367-9b6c-cab3191766f2", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Economic graphs and interpretation", "children": [{"id": "872f3b04-af6a-443e-93c2-fb3a805a3031", "type": "concept", "title": "Scatterplots and trend charts"}, {"id": "f67e3c1d-ca59-4186-8b38-d66ee95902b6", "type": "concept", "title": "Rates of change"}, {"id": "1ded62e8-9af3-40bc-81ad-d6b95353135a", "type": "concept", "title": "Correlation versus causation"}], "description": "The point is to explain relationships clearly without overstating causality."}, {"id": "d5619950-ddf6-4fac-8c1e-a14b0c282975", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Policy and business memos", "children": [{"id": "853a5cbd-61ae-435a-ac13-0f54aa9ee410", "type": "concept", "title": "Evidence summary"}, {"id": "57a10ae3-b931-4d48-8f2b-9dd38c094717", "type": "concept", "title": "Assumptions and uncertainty"}, {"id": "2e16baa8-378d-4faf-896c-ee7068293435", "type": "concept", "title": "Implications and action"}], "description": "Students write concise economic recommendations for managers or policymakers."}]}], "dbBacked": true}$mmecjson$::jsonb,
